OneiOS take18, userland/metal/patches/NativeMetal/0002: the 2 s idle trim of the runtime's kept memory runs.
Upstream: the fix of Droid-VM/NativeMetal 46fdc91 (UniXNU line, rponeawa, 2026-11-11: the memory pressure source held
only by a local never delivered an event) as the board's 935c468 (HuJK, 2026-11-16) applies it to this timer.
What: watchIdleMemory's dispatch timer is a static. The frontend is compiled with ARC; at b0d6a07 the timer was held only
by a local of its dispatch_once block, so its last reference went when the block returned and libdispatch took it off its
queue (_dispatch_source_xref_dispose, DQF_RELEASED): nmb_device_trim_memory(device, 2000) never ran in any process. The
pressure source next to it lives (its handler captures it). Each tick also calls oneios_idle_tick where the image has it
(userland/metal/Switches.inc: Turnip's freed-BO cache trimmed once a minute, mesa 0003).
Why: with the trim dead, the kept empty pooled blocks (board metal2vulkan 0013), the spare command pools (0022) and the
merge scratches (0030) were given back only at a memory pressure rise, never at idle: upstream OneiOS's render server held
2,600-3,400 blobs under 1 MiB given back only at a pressure rise (50873fe's message), every blob wired guest RAM.
Switch: boot argument oneios-idle-trim=0 (ONEIOS_IDLE_TRIM=0): no timer, as before. Removable: yes
(ONEIOS_METAL_SKIP=idle-trim-timer-lives). metal2vulkan 0006 and mesa 0003 act only through this timer.

diff --git a/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm b/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm
index b21ef41..b1f2c72 100644
--- a/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm
+++ b/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm
@@ -1166,13 +1166,26 @@ static void watchImportPressure() {
 // widget renderer its own. A pool whose placements come each frame refills its kept block within the frame, so only blocks no frame
 // asked for in two seconds go. (Waiting for the process to commit nothing for two seconds never trimmed the render server: the home
 // screen's clock keeps it drawing.)
+// The timer lives as long as the process (OneiOS; upstream 46fdc91's fix of the pressure source, done for this timer by the
+// board's 935c468): this file is compiled with ARC, and a dispatch source whose last reference goes is taken off its event queue
+// (libdispatch's _dispatch_source_xref_dispose, DQF_RELEASED). Held only by a local of the block below, as before, it was released
+// when the block returned and never fired: no kept block, spare command pool or merge scratch was ever trimmed at idle (the board's
+// metal2vulkan 0013, 0022, 0030), only at a memory pressure rise (whose source lives: its handler holds it). The boot argument
+// oneios-idle-trim=0 (ONEIOS_IDLE_TRIM=0, userland/metal/Switches.inc) starts no timer, as before. Each tick also calls
+// oneios_idle_tick where the image has it (userland/metal/Switches.inc: Turnip's idle trim of its freed-BO cache, once a minute).
+extern "C" void oneios_idle_tick(void) __attribute__((weak));
 static void watchIdleMemory() {
  static dispatch_once_t once;
+ static dispatch_source_t timer;
  dispatch_once(&once,^{
-  dispatch_source_t timer=dispatch_source_create(DISPATCH_SOURCE_TYPE_TIMER,0,0,dispatch_get_global_queue(QOS_CLASS_UTILITY,0));
+  if(const char *on=getenv("ONEIOS_IDLE_TRIM"))if(!strcmp(on,"0"))return;
+  timer=dispatch_source_create(DISPATCH_SOURCE_TYPE_TIMER,0,0,dispatch_get_global_queue(QOS_CLASS_UTILITY,0));
   if(!timer)return;
   dispatch_source_set_timer(timer,dispatch_time(DISPATCH_TIME_NOW,2*NSEC_PER_SEC),2*NSEC_PER_SEC,250*NSEC_PER_MSEC);
-  dispatch_source_set_event_handler(timer,^{if(gDevice)gTrimmedBlocks+=nmb_device_trim_memory(gDevice,2000);});
+  dispatch_source_set_event_handler(timer,^{
+   if(gDevice)gTrimmedBlocks+=nmb_device_trim_memory(gDevice,2000);
+   if(&oneios_idle_tick)oneios_idle_tick();
+  });
   dispatch_activate(timer);
  });
 }
